"§3, so no number §4 can be below §5.\n"
"\n"
"Prove that no such function exists. The statement is a negation, so assume you were handed one\n"
"and derive a contradiction: §6 names the supposed function and its supposed\n"
"property, and then you only have to ask §7 about the empty list."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `no_total_index : ¬∃ f : List ℕ → ℕ, ∀ xs, f xs < xs.length`
#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:26
msgid "§0\n"
"\n"
"No total function can return a valid index into every list, because the empty list has none."
msgstr ""

#: Game/Levels/Specification/L06_ASpecificationNothingCanSatisfy.lean:33
